From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Jim Martin <jimmartin@gmail.com>
Date: Thu, 8 Oct 2026 13:41:08 -0500
Subject: [PATCH] clk: qcom: gcc-glymur: Add the USB4 PHY and DP0 PHY resets

The reset map has the DP0 PHY reset of the first USB4 instance but not
those of the other two, and none of the USB4 PHY block resets. A USB4
host router has to reset its PHY as part of its startup sequence, which
it cannot do while the reset is missing here.

Add the five resets. Their registers are in the same PHY blocks as the
existing USB3 PHY and DP0 PHY resets.

Assisted-by: Opus 5.5
Signed-off-by: Jim Martin <jimmartin@gmail.com>
---
 drivers/clk/qcom/gcc-glymur.c | 5 +++++
 1 file changed, 5 insertions(+)

diff --git a/drivers/clk/qcom/gcc-glymur.c b/drivers/clk/qcom/gcc-glymur.c
index 341aff09650..07242a98a41 100644
--- a/drivers/clk/qcom/gcc-glymur.c
+++ b/drivers/clk/qcom/gcc-glymur.c
@@ -8341,6 +8341,11 @@ static const struct qcom_reset_map gcc_glymur_resets[] = {
 	[GCC_VIDEO_AXI1_CLK_ARES] = { 0x32044, 2 },
 	[GCC_VIDEO_BCR] = { 0x32000 },
 	[GCC_VIDEO_AXI0C_CLK_ARES] = { 0x32030, 2 },
+	[GCC_USB4PHY_0_PHY_PRIM_BCR] = { 0xdb01c },
+	[GCC_USB4PHY_1_PHY_SEC_BCR] = { 0x2c01c },
+	[GCC_USB4PHY_2_PHY_TERT_BCR] = { 0xbe01c },
+	[GCC_USB4_1_DP0_PHY_SEC_BCR] = { 0x2c010 },
+	[GCC_USB4_2_DP0_PHY_TERT_BCR] = { 0xbe010 },
 };
 
 static const struct clk_rcg_dfs_data gcc_dfs_clocks[] = {
